v1.3.0 (2026-05-11)
-------------------
- User self-registration via email invite: admin creates user, checks "Send registration
  link", user receives email with a time-limited token link (72h default, configurable)
- Registration page (/register?token=...): user clicks one button, server generates RSA
  cert, registers it to SoftEther, user downloads .p12 and .ovpn (OpenVPN Connect)
- Token lifecycle: pending → activated (cert generated) → used (p12 downloaded); token
  is marked used after p12 download; expired/reused tokens show error
- Resend invite: Edit User modal → Registration Invite section → Send Registration Link;
  invite status badge shown (Invite pending / Cert generated / Registered)
- User email stored in user_meta.json (separate from SoftEther, no API interference)
- vpnweb Settings: new sidebar nav item with SMTP config (host, port, STARTTLS/SSL,
  user, password, from address) and registration settings (token expiry, base URL)
- aiosmtplib used for async email delivery

v1.2.0 (2026-04-29)
-------------------
- Dual-address profiles: each profile now has a secondary hostname/port tried automatically
  if the primary is unreachable at login time
- Removed NAT-T hint support: host/hint format no longer parsed or stripped anywhere —
  hostname stored and used as-is in both JSON-RPC and vpncmd paths
- Fixed saveProfile: now checks HTTP response status and shows server error messages
- Added profiles gear button (⚙) to main screen sidebar — no need to disconnect to edit profiles

v1.1.0 (2026-04-29)
-------------------
- Changed listen port from 8443 to 8080 (HTTP, for HAProxy SSL termination upstream)
  Note: port 443 is occupied by SoftEther VPN server on the same host
- Renamed session cookie from "session" to "vpnweb_sid" (avoids HAProxy sticky-session conflict)
- Login endpoint switched to JSONResponse for reliable Set-Cookie delivery
- All fetch() calls now use credentials: 'include'
- Added 30-minute inactivity session timeout (auto-logout)

v1.0.0 (2026-04-28)
-------------------
Initial release.

Features:
- FastAPI + single-page JS frontend for SoftEther VPN management
- Direct JSON-RPC (httpx) and vpncmd subprocess fallback for relay servers
- Bulk endpoints /api/server/all and /api/hubs/{hub}/all (one round-trip load)
- Session management with inactivity timeout (cookie: vpnweb_sid)
- Connection profiles (profiles.json) with per-profile host/port
- VPN Azure toggle and hostname display (vpncmd fallback, JSON-RPC unsupported)
- Dynamic DNS hostname display
- SecureNAT / DHCP config with MAC address display
- User, group, session, MAC/IP table management per hub
- Cascade links, L3 switches, listeners, bridges
- IPSec, OpenVPN, syslog settings
- Hub create/delete, hub online/offline toggle
- SVG logo and favicon (blue gradient circle + padlock)
- vpncmd concurrency semaphore (max 2) for relay server compatibility
- Debug endpoints: /api/debug/ddns, /api/debug/hub/{hub}/users, /api/debug/vcmd
